WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
Every turn of the roundabout rebuilds four-carbon oxaloacetate.

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.080
That makes it a reusable platform, not a fuel.

3
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.480
So here is a puzzle.

4
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.540
If the platform always comes back, why does the cell spend ATP to make more of it?

5
00:00:19.933 --> 00:00:21.913
Because the roundabout has exits.

6
00:00:23.073 --> 00:00:27.093
The cycle is amphibolic: it serves both breakdown and building.

7
00:00:28.593 --> 00:00:30.333
Citrate leaves to make fatty acids.

8
00:00:31.733 --> 00:00:35.273
Alpha α-Ketoglutarate becomes glutamate and other amino acids.

9
00:00:36.673 --> 00:00:38.333
Succinyl-CoA builds heme.

10
00:00:39.393 --> 00:00:43.453
Oxaloacetate itself feeds gluconeogenesis, the making of new glucose.

11
00:00:44.633 --> 00:00:48.333
Each exit takes carbon that would have become oxaloacetate.

12
00:00:49.453 --> 00:00:52.333
If nothing replaces it, the platform pool shrinks.

13
00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:59.153
Citrate synthase, the step that starts each turn, is limited by oxaloacetate supply.

14
00:01:00.613 --> 00:01:02.253
So fewer acetyl groups can merge.

15
00:01:03.493 --> 00:01:06.973
The cycle slows, and fewer loaded carriers leave for the chain.

16
00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:11.853
Hans Krebs saw this pool at work in minced pigeon breast muscle.

17
00:01:13.013 --> 00:01:18.393
A pinch of a four-carbon acid made the muscle burn far more oxygen than that pinch

18
00:01:18.393 --> 00:01:24.193
could explain. Each added molecule joined the pool and carried many acetyl groups

19
00:01:24.193 --> 00:01:25.193
through.

20
00:01:26.717 --> 00:01:28.357
Here is the guiding idea.

21
00:01:29.817 --> 00:01:33.837
Oxaloacetate behaves as a catalyst only while nothing is drawn off.

22
00:01:35.057 --> 00:01:37.537
Whatever leaves for building must be put back.

23
00:01:38.777 --> 00:01:41.237
That refilling has a name: anaplerosis.

24
00:01:42.317 --> 00:01:46.857
In many tissues, the chief refill enzyme is pyruvate carboxylase.

25
00:01:48.057 --> 00:01:52.297
It adds CO₂ to pyruvate, making a new oxaloacetate.

26
00:01:53.397 --> 00:01:54.957
The reaction uses ATP.

27
00:01:56.257 --> 00:01:59.197
That is the ATP spent in the opening puzzle.

28
00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:04.920
Now predict. Pyruvate carboxylase needs an on switch.

29
00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:11.100
Which molecule, arriving at the roundabout's entrance, would make the most sensible

30
00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.720
signal to build more platform?

31
00:02:18.867 --> 00:02:21.407
Acetyl-CoA, the incoming fuel.

32
00:02:22.707 --> 00:02:26.147
When it is arriving, it switches pyruvate carboxylase on.

33
00:02:27.327 --> 00:02:28.867
This is feedforward control.

34
00:02:30.207 --> 00:02:34.087
The message reads: fuel is arriving, so build more of the platform.

35
00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.420
Pyruvate carboxylase is not the only way in.

36
00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:42.440
In dividing cells, glutamine is a major source.

37
00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.560
So a working cycle is a busy hub.

38
00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:51.380
Carbon leaves for building, refills come in, and the platform pool holds steady.

39
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.060
So the platform is reusable, but it is not untouchable.

40
00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:01.820
The roundabout loads electron carriers and supplies builders at the same time.

41
00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:05.900
What the builders take, anaplerosis must give back.
